# Masses are conserved across reactions: m(N2) = 2 m(N), m(O2) = 2 m(O),
# m(NO) = m(N) + m(O), and each ion is its neutral minus the electron
# mass.  A reaction whose products and reactants differ in mass changes
# the centre-of-mass kinetic energy at every event, so a gas that cycles
# through forward and reverse reactions does not conserve energy.

